    "q-182516": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182516",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q){{field-4}}Q\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P\\text{ }∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{T}∨\\text{T})∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{T}∨\\text{F})∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{F}∨\\text{T})∧¬(\\text{F}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)$ is logically equivalent to $Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)≡Q.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
